{"id":3881,"date":"2021-10-25T13:30:34","date_gmt":"2021-10-25T20:30:34","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=3881"},"modified":"2025-10-23T13:17:16","modified_gmt":"2025-10-23T20:17:16","slug":"0-1-connecting-and-coding-with-cde-blockly","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/0-1-connecting-and-coding-with-cde-blockly\/","title":{"rendered":"1.1: Connecting and Coding with Blockly"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213305a909\" name=\"6a2213305a909\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>We've Moved!<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text css=&#8221;.vc_custom_1761250634457{background-color: #ffdddd !important;border-radius: 3px !important;}&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-11766\" src=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/06\/icon_warning-150x150-2-84x85.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"81\" height=\"82\" \/><\/p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\"><strong>We\u2019ve moved to our new lesson portal: <a href=\"http:\/\/learn.robolink.com\">Robolink Learn<\/a>! Lessons here will remain available until the end of June 2026. This version of Basecamp will no longer be updated and uses outdated references to Blockly for Robolink. You can access the previous version of <a href=\"https:\/\/codrone.robolink.com\/edu\/blockly-archive\/\">Blockly here<\/a>.<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213305adc5\" name=\"6a2213305adc5\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>What is Blockly?<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https:\/\/codrone.robolink.com\/edu\/blockly-archive\/\">Blockly<\/a> is an online application that you can access right from Google Chrome. You can go to it by heading to this URL:<a href=\"https:\/\/codrone.robolink.com\/edu\/blockly-archive\/\">https:\/\/codrone.robolink.com\/edu\/blockly-archive\/robolink.com\/blockly-cde<\/a>. <\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0With Blockly, you can connect it to your drone as well as program it in two modes:<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><strong>Junior:<\/strong> Simplified block-based coding for beginners<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><strong>Senior:<\/strong> For intermediate coders who have some familiarity with block coding <\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>There is no need to install anything since Blockly runs only in the browser![\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;12841&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213305ae42\" name=\"6a2213305ae42\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Google Chrome Version<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Your Google Chrome should be updated to the most recent version. If you are not sure how to check, click on the menu on the top right, scroll down to &#8220;Help&#8221;, and select &#8220;About Google Chrome&#8221;. Google Chrome might automatically update. If not, please update Chrome.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;2268&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;2267&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213305ae95\" name=\"6a2213305ae95\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Connect Your Controller over Micro USB<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_single_image image=&#8221;7150&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]Try to use the cable that comes with CoDrone EDU whenever possible! This Micro USB cable can transfer data, which is necessary for programming. Most Micro USB cables now are data compatible. <strong>If your drone does not switch to LINK state when connecting, you may have the wrong cable, or it may be broken.<\/strong>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;8764&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213305aee6\" name=\"6a2213305aee6\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Power on the Drone<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Next, power on the drone using a charged battery.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;4616&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Your drone should pair to the controller, as indicated by the solid LED on the drone and controller.<\/span><\/p>\n<p>**<em>If your drone and controller are not paired, watch <a href=\"https:\/\/youtu.be\/X-gyVk0YlzE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">this<\/a> video.<\/em>**[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213305af32\" name=\"6a2213305af32\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Connect the Controller to Blockly<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Once your controller is connected, click on the green &#8220;Connect&#8221; button on the bottom left of the screen. Then select the option from the drop-down menu. If you don&#8217;t see anything in the menu, check that your controller is in &#8220;LINK&#8221; state or use a different cable.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;12853&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]If you are still having trouble with connecting to Blockly, please read this article for help: <a href=\"https:\/\/robolink.helpdocs.io\/article\/wti0fkm5ya-help-blockly-is-not-pairing-to-my-co-drone-edu-controller\">Help! Blockly is not connecting to my CoDrone EDU controller!<\/a>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213305af9c\" name=\"6a2213305af9c\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Write Code<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<h3>Selecting a Block<\/h3>\n<p>To write your code, drag blocks from the menus on the left to the workspace in the middle of the page. Try dragging a <strong>take off<\/strong> block from the flight commands menu.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;12858&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<h3>Connecting Blocks<\/h3>\n<p>Connect a second block by dragging the block underneath the previous one until you see the yellow outline. For example, attach a <strong>land<\/strong> block.<\/p>\n<p>* <em>Click!<\/em> *[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;12860&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<h3>Deleting a Block<\/h3>\n<p>There are two ways to delete a block. The first way is to separate what you want to get rid of from your code and drag them to the trash can in the lower right-hand corner. To delete the entire program, you can drag all blocks at once to the trashcan.[\/vc_column_text][vc_column_text]You can also delete a block by dragging it to the left-hand side and dropping it in the menu.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;12861&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213305aff6\" name=\"6a2213305aff6\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 8<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Start Block<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]If you have used other visual programming interfaces before, you may be familiar with a <strong>when play clicked<\/strong> block similar to the one below.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;13292&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<p>Any blocks connected to this block will run when you click the &#8220;play&#8221; button, which is indicated by the text &#8220;Run code&#8221;.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;13283&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]Any blocks that are not connected to the <strong><em>when play clicked<\/em><\/strong> block will be automatically disabled.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;13287&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]Using this block is a useful feature if you want to quickly switch between multiple programs in your workspace.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;12709&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<strong>Note:<\/strong> <em>Using this block is optional. If you want to delete the block, Blockly will have to reload the page, and you will need to pair your drone again.<\/em>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213305b04a\" name=\"6a2213305b04a\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 9<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Other Resources<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<h3>Lessons<\/h3>\n<p>Select the &#8220;Lessons&#8221; tab on the right-hand side of Blockly to access the lessons. Now you can see your code and the tutorial at the same time![\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;12864&#8243; img_size=&#8221;2000&#215;2300&#8243; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<h3>Python Example<\/h3>\n<p>Select the &#8220;Python&#8221; tab from the right-hand side of Blockly to see what your block code would look like in Python. You can&#8217;t write any code in Python on the web just yet, but you can get a preview of Python coding and familiarize yourself with the language.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;13289&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213305b095\" name=\"6a2213305b095\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 10<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Run Code<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]When you are ready to run your program, place your drone\u00a0on the floor in an open area. <strong>Keep your drone controller connected to the computer.<\/strong> Then, click on &#8220;Run&#8221; on the upper left-hand side of your workspace.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;12842&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text css=&#8221;.vc_custom_1725565693567{background-color: #ffdddd !important;border-radius: 3px !important;}&#8221;]<img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-6153\" src=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/03\/icon_warning-300x300.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"58\" height=\"58\" srcset=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/03\/icon_warning-300x300.png 300w, https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/03\/icon_warning-150x150.png 150w, https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/03\/icon_warning.png 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 58px) 100vw, 58px\" \/>If you ever need to emergency stop your program for any reason, press the \u201cStop\u201d button in the top left corner of the workspace to stop the motors from spinning. Otherwise, select \u201cLand\u201d at any time to safely land the drone mid-flight.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 11 We've Moved! [vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1761250634457{background-color: #ffdddd !important;border-radius: 3px !important;}\"] We\u2019ve moved to our new lesson portal: Robolink Learn! Lessons here will remain available until the end of June&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/0-1-connecting-and-coding-with-cde-blockly\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":4741,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"easy","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":3877,"_lesson_preview":""},"lesson-category":[],"lesson-tag":[2108,4328,14401,2177,2122],"class_list":["post-3881","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-blockly","lesson-tag-cde","lesson-tag-cdej","lesson-tag-getting-started","lesson-tag-programming","module-beginner","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/3881","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":85,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/3881\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":13614,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/3881\/revisions\/13614"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"em